{
  "id": "cluster-randomization",
  "term": "cluster randomization",
  "definition": "Cluster randomization is a study design in which groups, or clusters, rather than individual people are assigned during an evaluation of interventions such as health-care, screening, or educational programs. In this approach, the sizes of the groups may differ, which can matter when planning the study.",
