      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly state the core defining feature that, in cluster randomization, clusters/groups are assigned rather than individual people; it only discusses the use of “cluster randomization design” and planning considerations for unequal cluster sizes.",
        "The packet mentions evaluation of health-care, screening (“screeening” in text), and educational interventions, but the definition’s broader phrasing about assignment “during an evaluation of interventions such as…” is only partially supported.",
        "The packet supports that cluster sizes can differ and that this can matter for planning/sample size calculations (it notes discrepancies in cluster sizes and that planning may use an average cluster size), but this support does not cover the definition’s unquoted assignment-vs-individuals framing."
